<GraphParameter name="SANDBOX_PATH" public="true" required="true"/>
<GraphParameter name="SANDBOX_NAME" public="true">
<attr name="dynamicValue"><![CDATA[//#CTL2

function string getValue() {
	string sandbox = getParamValue("SANDBOX_PATH");
	if (endsWith(sandbox,"/")) {sandbox = left(sandbox,(length(sandbox)-1));}
	integer sandboxIndex = 1 + lastIndexOf(sandbox,"/");
	sandbox = right(sandbox,length(sandbox)-sandboxIndex);
	return sandbox;
}
]]></attr>
</GraphParameter>
<GraphParameter name="FILE_NAME" public="true"/>
</GraphParameters>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="3465A4" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="150" id="Note_DebugInput" textColor="FFFFFF" width="310" x="-300" y="25">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Debug Input (standalone testing only)
Feeds test lines directly into the subgraph when run standalone in Designer.
Ignored when called from redactFile.grf — the parent graph supplies the input instead.
Points to: urlRedactionDebugInput.csv]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="9B59B6" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="150" id="Note_CSVBootstrap" textColor="FFFFFF" width="476" x="200" y="275">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Step 1 — Load configuration lists from CSV
Two CSV files are read once at startup and collapsed into single list-field records:
* *urlProperties.csv* — 35 property names to check (fileURL, transformURL, ldapUrl, etc.)
* *sensitiveQueryParams.csv* — 39 query param names to redact (password, api_key, access_token, etc.)
Dedup removes any duplicates. Denormalizer collapses all rows into one record containing a list.
To add a new property or param name: edit the CSV — no code changes needed.]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="9B59B6" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="125" id="Note_CrossJoin" textColor="FFFFFF" width="300" x="800" y="450">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Step 2 — CrossJoin
Attaches both lists to every incoming file line.
Each output record carries: lineContent, fileURL, propertiesList, sensitiveParamsList.
The CSVs are only read once — not once per line.]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="9B59B6" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="225" id="Note_PartitionMaps" textColor="FFFFFF" width="475" x="1175" y="-50">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Step 3 — Partition + Redaction Maps
The Partition routes each line based on its source file extension:
* *.cfg files* → REDACT_CFG (Java properties format: property=value)
* *Everything else* → REDACT_XML (.grf, .sgrf, .jbf, .rjob, .prm — XML format: property="value")

Both Maps apply the same protocol-aware redaction logic:
* Credentials in URL authority (user:pass@host) → replaced with REDACTED@host
* Sensitive query params (password=, api_key=, access_token= etc.) → value replaced with REDACTED
* Safe URLs (${...} refs, sandbox://, file:/, hdfs://) → left entirely unchanged
* zip/gzip wrappers and proxy wrappers → unwrapped, inner URL redacted, rebuilt

Port 0 out: the (possibly modified) line content
Port 1 out: a sanitisation report record for every line]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="9B59B6" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="125" id="Note_Output" textColor="FFFFFF" width="350" x="1325" y="475">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Output
*Port 0* — Sanitised line content. Flows back to redactFile.grf to be written into the output ZIP.
*Port 1* — Sanitisation report records. One per line processed. Aggregated into the RedactionReport CSV/XLSX in the final ZIP.]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
<RichTextNote backgroundColor="27AE60" folded="false" fontSize="medium" height="150" id="Note_TestHarness" textColor="FFFFFF" width="580" x="1770" y="-100">
<attr name="text"><![CDATA[h3. Automated Test Harness (debug only — inactive in production)
Verifies both outputs against known-good expected CSVs every time the subgraph is run standalone.
*Lines test:* actual output vs urlRedactionDebugOutput.csv — fails if any line was incorrectly redacted or left unchanged.
*Report test:* actual report vs urlRedactionDebugReportOutput.csv — fails if any report record is wrong.
DataIntersection routes mismatches to Fail (test fails) and matches to Success (test passes).
All components here are marked debugOutput=true and are invisible when called from redactFile.grf.]]></attr>
</RichTextNote>
